sk (`worktrees.py` already isolates per-session).\n- **[DO NOT SHIP default]** Wave-DAG / worktree-band parallelism â€” gain only on the minority of plans with independent bands, after merge+re-gate tax; forfeits the single-checkpoint/single-branch resume guarantee.\n- **[REJECT]** Speculative/parallel EXECUTE & cross-wave pipelining â€” violates the ascending truth-gate; ~2Ã— tokens, anti-lever under quota.\n- **[REJECT]** Shrinking the gate of record to \"impacted tests only\" â€” that *is* the vacuous-GREEN attack the full-suite gate exists to close. Affected-tests checks are allowed only as an inner-loop accelerator; **gate of record stays the full suite**.\n\n## Locked planning requirements (the cheap-reviewer lever)\n- **Q1 (good enough?)** The reviewer is *not* the correctness arbiter â€” the orchestrator-run full-suite **test gate** is. Keep one reviewer strong, make only the second cheap (a BLOCKER needs â‰¥2 agreement, so a cheap second can only *fail to confirm*, never raise a false blocker alone). Promote the cheap tier only if measured **recall â‰¥ a pre-registered threshold** over a shadow period + historical known-bad diffs.\n- **Q2 (stuck on a low tier?)** Never hard-code a model id â€” resolve reviewer by **tier/policy** at run time (same discipline as `REVIEWER_COUNT`). Add a staleness guard + scheduled re-calibration on model-release trigger (a natural `/schedule`/healthcheck owner).\n\n## Citation integrity\n- **[CORROBORATED]** \"Anthropic + Cognition agree\" = 2 genuinely independent origins (opposite priors, no cross-citation), *not* a bandwagon â€” but neither has **OBSERVED** parallel-code-writing data, so that sub-claim is opinion-corroborated, not OBSERVED. SKILL.md over-generalizes by citing Anthropic (whose own system parallelizes read-only research for a 90% cut) as an anti-parallel witness; the defensible claim is the narrower shared-mutation one.\n\n---\n\nOne flag worth your call: this template normally has the documents injected inl